  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRRS DRC 2026 &#x2013; UNICEF Urban WASH and Cholera Expert</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the early 1970s, cholera has posed a significant and persistent public health challenge in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC). In particular, certain lakeside areas within the Great Lakes Region have experienced nearly continuous transmission, serving as endemic zones and primary sources for the spread of outbreaks to other vulnerable regions.The situation in mid-end of 2025 is especially concerning. As of July 27 (epidemiological week 30), a total of 42,309 cases and 1,135 deaths have been reported &#x2014; nearly double the 22,148 cases and 295 deaths recorded during the same period in 2024.In recent weeks, the outbreak has intensified in western parts of the country, including Kinshasa &#x2014; the capital and one of the world&#x2019;s fastest-growing megacities.</narrative>
  </description>
